@prefix agp: <https://dagalog.no/ns/agentprov#> .
@prefix bl: <https://dagalog.no/ns/backlog#> .
@prefix ghissues: <https://github.com/daghovland/rdf-datalog/issues/> .
@prefix ghpull: <https://github.com/daghovland/rdf-datalog/pull/> .
@prefix prov: <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix session: <https://dagalog.no/ns/agentprov/session#> .

# PROSPECTIVE summary scaffold, generated by scripts/new-provenance-summary.sh.
# TODO: replace the placeholder summaryText/decisionPoint below with the
# actual distilled reasoning behind this PR before committing — see
# docs/plans/TRANSCRIPT_SUMMARY_GUIDELINES.md. Timestamps below are real
# (from `git log 4076b2aaa27be733b2b32f82e92afbf623937361..HEAD` on branch 489-done-column-query); everything else that
# isn't marked TODO can be left as-is.

ghpull:803 a bl:PullRequest, bl:WorkItem ;
    rdfs:label "backlog dashboard: board gets a Closed column + hideable columns (#489)" ;
    bl:number 803 ;
    bl:state bl:Open ;
    bl:closesIssue ghissues:489 .

session:claudeSonnet5 a prov:SoftwareAgent ;
    rdfs:label "Claude Sonnet 5" .

session:pr803 a agp:AgentSession ;
    prov:wasAssociatedWith session:claudeSonnet5 ;
    prov:used ghissues:489 ;
    prov:startedAtTime "2026-11-15T12:32:39Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    prov:endedAtTime "2026-11-15T12:32:39Z"^^xsd:dateTime .

session:pr803Summary a agp:TranscriptSummary ;
    agp:summaryText "Issue #489 noted the backlog dashboard's Board tab \"Done\" column was effectively always empty: loadBoard() in backlog_endpoint/src/backlog_frontend.html queried only bl:state bl:Open, but per CLAUDE.md's workflow bl:status bl:Done means 'PR open, CI green, awaiting merge' while the issue is still bl:state bl:Open -- the moment the PR actually merges the issue flips to bl:state bl:Closed and vanishes from the query entirely, so Done only ever showed content in the narrow pre-merge window. The issue body offered two framed options (time-windowed Done column, or a separate time-windowed 'recently shipped' view) and asked for a decision. Before implementing either, checked the issue's GitHub comment thread and found Dag had posted a follow-up comment (https://github.com/daghovland/rdf-datalog/issues/489#issuecomment-5302244166) after the issue body that superseded that framing entirely: derive board columns dynamically from the bl:status values actually present in the data, add an always-visible Closed column with no time window at all, and make every column hideable via a persisted per-viewer preference, deferring a separate column-rename question pending his own confirmation. The Agent status was set three days after that comment, so it authorizes the comment's design, not the stale issue-body framing." ;
    agp:reasoningFor ghpull:803 ;
    agp:decisionPoint session:pr803Decision ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy session:pr803 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo session:claudeSonnet5 .

session:pr803Decision a agp:Decision ;
    agp:summaryText "Rewrote loadBoard() to run two small queries (open issues with status; closed non-epic issues) mirroring PR #429's established 'small unparameterized queries, join client-side' pattern for this file, deriving columns from whatever bl:status values are actually present (known vocabulary order, unknown values appended) plus an always-present Closed column with no recency filter. Added per-column hide/show checkboxes persisted to localStorage key backlog-board-hidden-columns, wrapped in try/catch per this file's existing defensive-storage convention. Verified against the real local dataset (scripts/serve-backlog.sh): extracted the exact SPARQL query strings from the committed JS via a small Node harness and POSTed them to a running endpoint rather than trusting a read-through, confirming 207 closed non-epic issues -- previously invisible -- now populate the Closed column. Filed #801 (Status Todo) for the deferred column-rename mechanism (canonical rdfs:label vs. a personal override), since Dag's comment explicitly said that part still needs his own confirmation before implementation, per CLAUDE.md's 'follow-up work must become a real issue' rule." ;
    agp:alternative "The issue body's literal 'option 1' (keep a single Done column, widen it with a ~14-day recency window on recently-closed bl:status bl:Done issues) was the originally-briefed approach but was deliberately not built: Dag's own later comment on the issue explicitly moved past that two-option framing to the dynamic-columns design implemented here, and the Agent status authorization postdates that comment. Building the literal option 1 instead would have contradicted the issue owner's own documented decision and mis-recorded a superseded alternative as though it were a live tradeoff." .
